{"id":"mahabharata-1-214","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":214,"title":"चतुर्दशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 214 · Agni comes to Krishna and Arjuna","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas rule prosperously, and Krishna and Arjuna go to the Yamuna for pleasure near the Khandava forest. A tall, radiant Brahmin approaches them and asks for food.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ಸಮೃದ್ಧಿಯಿಂದ ಆಳುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣಾರ್ಜುನರು ವಿಹಾರಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಖಾಂಡವವನದ ಬಳಿ ಯಮುನೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಎತ್ತರದ ತೇಜಸ್ವಿ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನೊಬ್ಬನು ಅವರನ್ನು ಸಮೀಪಿಸಿ ಆಹಾರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव समृद्धि से शासन करते हैं, और श्रीकृष्ण तथा अर्जुन विहार के लिए खाण्डव वन के पास यमुना जाते हैं। एक लम्बा, तेजस्वी ब्राह्मण उनके पास आकर भोजन माँगता है।","te":"పాండవులు సమృద్ధిగా పాలిస్తారు; శ్రీకృష్ణార్జునులు విహారం కోసం ఖాండవవనం దగ్గర యమునకు వెళ్తారు. పొడవైన తేజస్వి బ్రాహ్మణుడు ఒకడు వారిని సమీపించి ఆహారం అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் செழிப்புடன் ஆள, ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரும் அர்ஜுனனும் உலாவுவதற்காகக் காண்டவ வனத்தருகே யமுனைக்குச் செல்கிறார்கள். உயர்ந்த, ஒளிமிக்க அந்தணர் ஒருவர் அவர்களை அணுகி உணவு கேட்கிறார்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ സമൃദ്ധിയോടെ ഭരിക്കുന്നു; ആനന്ദത്തിനായി കൃഷ്ണനും അർജുനനും ഖാണ്ഡവവനത്തിനടുത്തുള്ള യമുനയിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു. ഉയരമുള്ള, തേജസ്സുള്ള ഒരു ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ അവരെ സമീപിച്ച് ഭക്ഷണം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.214; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"खाण्डवदाहपर्व","titleEn":"Khandavadaha Parva (Burning of the Khandava forest)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इन्द्रप्रस्थे वसन्तस्ते जघ्नुरन्यान्नराधिपान् ।\nशासनाद्धृतराष्ट्रस्य राज्ञः शांतनवस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living at Indraprastha, they subdued other kings, by the command of King Dhritarashtra and of Shantanu's son Bhishma."}},{"n":2,"text":"आश्रित्य धर्मराजानं सर्वलोकोऽवसत्सुखम् ।\nपुण्यलक्षणकर्माणं स्वदेहमिव देहिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the world lived happily in the shelter of the Dharma-king, whose deeds bore the marks of merit, as embodied beings live in their own body."}},{"n":3,"text":"स समं धर्मकामार्थान्सिषेवे भरतर्षभः ।\nत्रीनिवात्मसमान्बन्धून्बन्धुमानिव मानयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That bull of the Bharatas served dharma, profit and desire equally, honoring the three as a man with kin honors three relatives dear as himself."}},{"n":4,"text":"तेषां समविभक्तानां क्षितौ देहवतामिव ।\nबभौ धर्मार्थकामानां चतुर्थ इव पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those three, equally divided like embodied beings on earth, the king shone as if he were a fourth."}},{"n":5,"text":"अध्येतारं परं वेदाः प्रयोक्तारं महाध्वराः ।\nरक्षितारं शुभं वर्णा लेभिरे तं जनाधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vedas found in him the best student, the great sacrifices a performer, and the classes of society a good protector of that king of men."}},{"n":6,"text":"अधिष्ठानवती लक्ष्मीः परायणवती मतिः ।\nबन्धुमानखिलो धर्मस्तेनासीत्पृथिवीक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fortune had a foundation, intelligence a refuge, and all dharma a kinsman, in that ruler of the earth."}},{"n":7,"text":"भ्रातृभिः सहितो राजा चतुर्भिरधिकं बभौ ।\nप्रयुज्यमानैर्विततो वेदैरिव महाध्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his four brothers the king shone the more, like a great sacrifice spread out with the Vedas in use."}},{"n":8,"text":"तं तु धौम्यादयो विप्राः परिवार्योपतस्थिरे ।\nबृहस्पतिसमा मुख्याः प्रजापतिमिवामराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins led by Dhaumya, the foremost, equal to Brihaspati, attended him all around, as the immortals attend Prajapati."}},{"n":9,"text":"धर्मराजे अतिप्रीत्या पूर्णचन्द्र इवामले ।\nप्रजानां रेमिरे तुल्यं नेत्राणि हृदयानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Dharma-king, spotless like the full moon, the eyes and hearts of the people delighted in equal measure."}},{"n":10,"text":"न तु केवलदैवेन प्रजा भावेन रेमिरे ।\nयद्बभूव मनःकान्तं कर्मणा स चकार तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people did not delight merely by fate or feeling; whatever pleased their minds, he made real by his deeds."}},{"n":11,"text":"न ह्ययुक्तं न चासत्यं नानृतं न च विप्रियम् ।\nभाषितं चारुभाषस्य जज्ञे पार्थस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No improper, untrue, false or unpleasant word was ever spoken by the wise Partha of the graceful speech."}},{"n":12,"text":"स हि सर्वस्य लोकस्य हितमात्मन एव च ।\nचिकीर्षुः सुमहातेजा रेमे भरतसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Desiring the good of all the world and of himself, that best of the Bharatas, of great radiance, was happy."}},{"n":13,"text":"तथा तु मुदिताः सर्वे पाण्डवा विगतज्वराः ।\nअवसन्पृथिवीपालांस्त्रासयन्तः स्वतेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus all the Pandavas lived joyful and free of fever, terrifying the rulers of the earth by their splendor."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः कतिपयाहस्य बीभत्सुः कृष्णमब्रवीत् ।\nउष्णानि कृष्ण वर्तन्ते गच्छामो यमुनां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after some days, Bibhatsu said to Krishna: The days are hot, Krishna; let us go to the Yamuna."}},{"n":15,"text":"सुहृज्जनवृतास्तत्र विहृत्य मधुसूदन ।\nसायाह्ने पुनरेष्यामो रोचतां ते जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let us amuse ourselves there with our friends, Madhusudana, and return in the evening, if it pleases you, Janardana."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"कुन्तीमातर्ममाप्येतद्रोचते यद्वयं जले ।\nसुहृज्जनवृताः पार्थ विहरेम यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, this pleases me too: let us play in the water with our friends as we like."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"आमन्त्र्य धर्मराजानमनुज्ञाप्य च भारत ।\nजग्मतुः पार्थगोविन्दौ सुहृज्जनवृतौ ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking leave of the Dharma-king and receiving his permission, Partha and Govinda then went, surrounded by friends."}},{"n":18,"text":"विहारदेशं संप्राप्य नानाद्रुमवदुत्तमम् ।\nगृहैरुच्चावचैर्युक्तं पुरंदरगृहोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the pleasure ground, excellent with many kinds of trees and equipped with houses of every sort, like the house of Purandara,"}},{"n":19,"text":"भक्ष्यैर्भोज्यैश्च पेयैश्च रसवद्भिर्महाधनैः ।\nमाल्यैश्च विविधैर्युक्तं युक्तं वार्ष्णेयपार्थयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"supplied with food, drink and costly delicacies, and with many kinds of garlands, prepared for Vrishni and Partha,"}},{"n":20,"text":"आविवेशतुरापूर्णं रत्नैरुच्चावचैः शुभैः ।\nयथोपजोषं सर्वश्च जनश्चिक्रीड भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"they entered it, filled with fine and various jewels, and all the people there amused themselves as they liked, O Bharata."}},{"n":21,"text":"वने काश्चिज्जले काश्चित्काश्चिद्वेश्मसु चाङ्गनाः ।\nयथादेशं यथाप्रीति चिक्रीडुः कृष्णपार्थयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some women played in the forest, some in the water, some in the houses, each where and as she pleased, in the company of Krishna and Partha."}},{"n":22,"text":"द्रौपदी च सुभद्रा च वासांस्याभरणानि च ।\nप्रयच्छेतां महार्हाणि स्त्रीणां ते स्म मदोत्कटे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi and Subhadra gave costly garments and ornaments to the women, who were wild with drink."}},{"n":23,"text":"काश्चित्प्रहृष्टा ननृतुश्चुक्रुशुश्च तथापराः ।\nजहसुश्चापरा नार्यः पपुश्चान्या वरासवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some, delighted, danced; others shouted; some women laughed and others drank fine wine."}},{"n":24,"text":"रुरुदुश्चापरास्तत्र प्रजघ्नुश्च परस्परम् ।\nमन्त्रयामासुरन्याश्च रहस्यानि परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some wept there, some struck each other, and others whispered secrets to each other."}},{"n":25,"text":"वेणुवीणामृदङ्गानां मनोज्ञानां च सर्वशः ।\nशब्देनापूर्यते ह स्म तद्वनं सुसमृद्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wealthy grove was filled with the sounds of flutes, vinas and drums, pleasing in every way."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा वर्तमाने कुरुदाशार्हनन्दनौ ।\nसमीपे जग्मतुः कंचिदुद्देशं सुमनोहरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While this went on, the two joys of the Kurus and of the Dasharhas went to a lovely spot near by."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्र गत्वा महात्मानौ कृष्णौ परपुरंजयौ ।\nमहार्हासनयो राजंस्ततस्तौ संनिषीदतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there, the two great-souled Krishnas, conquerors of enemy cities, sat down, O king, on costly seats."}},{"n":28,"text":"तत्र पूर्वव्यतीतानि विक्रान्तानि रतानि च ।\nबहूनि कथयित्वा तौ रेमाते पार्थमाधवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they delighted, recalling many deeds of valor and pleasures of the past, Partha and Madhava."}},{"n":29,"text":"तत्रोपविष्टौ मुदितौ नाकपृष्ठेऽश्विनाविव ।\nअभ्यगच्छत्तदा विप्रो वासुदेवधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seated there happily, like the two Ashvins on the heights of heaven, Vasudeva and Dhananjaya were then approached by a Brahmin."}},{"n":30,"text":"बृहच्छालप्रतीकाशः प्रतप्तकनकप्रभः ।\nहरिपिङ्गो हरिश्मश्रुः प्रमाणायामतः समः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was tall as a great sala tree, bright as molten gold, tawny, with a tawny beard, of just proportion in height."}},{"n":31,"text":"तरुणादित्यसंकाशः कृष्णवासा जटाधरः ।\nपद्मपत्राननः पिङ्गस्तेजसा प्रज्वलन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He shone like the young sun, dressed in black, wearing matted locks, lotus-leaf faced, ruddy and blazing as it were with radiance."}},{"n":32,"text":"उपसृष्टं तु तं कृष्णौ भ्राजमानं द्विजोत्तमम् ।\nअर्जुनो वासुदेवश्च तूर्णमुत्पत्य तस्थतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that best of Brahmins, radiant, approach them, Arjuna and Vasudeva quickly sprang up and stood."}}]}]}